<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Programming Concepts</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #f5f3ff;
            padding: 30px;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 850px;
            margin: auto;
            background: white;
            padding: 30px;
            border-radius: 15px;
        }

        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #5b35b5;
        }

        .concept {
            padding: 18px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            background: #f1edff;
            border-radius: 10px;
        }

        h2 {
            color: #5b35b5;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container">

    <h1>👨‍💻 Basic Programming Concepts</h1>

    <div class="concept">
        <h2>1. Variable</h2>
        <p>A variable stores information that can be used by a program.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="concept">
        <h2>2. Data Type</h2>
        <p>Data types define what kind of value a variable can store.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="concept">
        <h2>3. Conditional Statement</h2>
        <p>Conditional statements allow a program to make decisions.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="concept">
        <h2>4. Loop</h2>
        <p>A loop repeats a set of instructions multiple times.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="concept">
        <h2>5. Function</h2>
        <p>A function is a reusable block of code designed to perform a task.</p>
    </div>

</div>

</body>
</html>
